6664b362b3b4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4d7d656b331745b1f2dd2979cabc6664b362b3b4.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 16 at 6:36PM MDT until August 16 at 9:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 636 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1.5 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nBox Elder Creek, Sanborn Draw, South Platte River, Crow Creek and\nLost Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nKersey, Riverside Reservoir, Hardin and Masters.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8cb7fcbb719c441287c4ec832c9b303e0f92090a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8cb7fcbb719c441287c4ec832c9b303e0f92090a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-16T23:59:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 162359 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 559 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered thunderstorms possible through this evening. A few of them could become strong to severe, with strong winds, large hail, and heavy rainfall. - Warming and drying trend for Monday and Tuesday, but still isolated gusty pm storms/virga. - More activ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-16T18:48:0